Subject: [LOCAL DIAGNOSTIC] PCI: qcom: report suspend branch and ICC teardown

Diagnostic only. This does not claim to fix L2 entry or CXSD.
Log state without accessing DBI after PME_Turn_Off. Remove after testing;
printk may itself perturb suspend timing. Based on pristine Linux v7.3.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2350,12 +2350,18 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	dev_info(dev, "CXSD audit: suspended=%d skip_pwrctrl_off=%d use_pm_opp=%d target=%d\n",
+		 pcie->pci->suspended, pcie->pci->pp.skip_pwrctrl_off,
+		 pcie->use_pm_opp, pm_suspend_target_state);
+
 	if (pcie->pci->suspended) {
 		ret = icc_disable(pcie->icc_mem);
+		dev_info(dev, "CXSD audit: icc_mem disable=%d\n", ret);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable PCIe-MEM interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
 
 		ret = icc_disable(pcie->icc_cpu);
+		dev_info(dev, "CXSD audit: icc_cpu disable=%d\n", ret);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
 
